                <pb facs="0107" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.001/423: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Chefoo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Roberts</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-15T13:00:00-05:00">December 15, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Reference your No. 6, December 12, 3 p.m. The Department desires that you
                    follow the situation closely and that you report promptly by telegraph whether
                    or not the restrictions have in actual practice been removed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
